@startuml interrupt_priority
!theme plain
title Simultaneous Interrupt Detection & Resolution

|loop()|
start
:Multiple interrupts may\nfire simultaneously;

partition "Simultaneous Interrupt Resolution" #LightBlue {
  :Check **buttonFlag**\n(portENTER_CRITICAL);
  if (buttonFlag?) then (yes)
    #Orange:processButtonInterrupt()
    **HIGHEST PRIORITY**
    Toggles blinking mode
    Cancels all lower modes;
  else (no)
  endif

  :Check **distance sensor**\n(polled measurement);
  if (object < 20cm && !blinkingMode?) then (yes)
    #Yellow:processDistanceSensor()
    **MEDIUM PRIORITY**
    Sets TL-B opposite to TL-A
    Overrides timer control of TL-B;
  else (no)
  endif

  :Check **timerFlag**\n(portENTER_CRITICAL);
  if (timerFlag && !blinkingMode?) then (yes)
    #LightGreen:processTimerInterrupt()
    **LOWEST PRIORITY**
    Advances TL-A state machine
    Skipped if override/blink active;
  else (no)
  endif
}

:delay(50ms);
stop

note right
  **Resource Protection:**
  - portMUX critical sections
    for atomic flag access
  - volatile flags set in ISRs
  - Deferred processing in loop()

  **Nested Interrupts (real HW):**
  - Timer ISR: Level 1
  - Button ISR: Level 3
  - Button can preempt timer
end note

|loop()|

@enduml
